         t_resp = 17 + 0.5 + 104.8 + 0.3 us = 122.6 us (CONDITIONAL on S2's sense delay and tPD(MR)); W140's and W145's chain (RESET1
           through 750 Ohm onto NRST, withdrawn: it latches with a hold stage, W145-F1) read 157.4 us of NRST fall and 174.7 us
       the reset hold (SESSION W148-1, replacing W145-1's CTR1 capacitor): TPS3703F6050DSER with CT pulled to its VDD through 10k 1% (TI 7.3
         note 1: a pull-up 'is required, 10 kOhm is recommended'; 9.1.2.1: the factory-programmed timing), option F's delay tD 14 / 20 /
         26 ms (7.6, p.7, PRINTED), after 'After MR returns to a logic high and the SENSE pin voltage is within a valid window ... RESET is deasserted after the reset delay time (tD).' (8.3.5, p.16; Figure 8-2's note B: 'To initiate and continue time reset counter both conditions must be met MR pin above VMR_H or floating'; note C: 'MR is ignored during output RESET low event').
         The 14 ms after MR is PRINTED BY REFERENCE (W150's F6): tD(MR)'s row, 'MR reset time delay', prints 'tD' in its NOM column
