         TI prints no condition on the fault's length beyond tMR_W: the hold is a timer, not a capacitor's discharge (9.1.2.1 against
         9.1.2.2's capacitor option, which this draft does not use). Its SENSE sits on its own VDD, so 'The configuration of the CT pin is re-evaluated by the device every time the voltage on the SENSE line enters the valid window' (8.3.4, p.15) happens at
         the part's own start and SENSE never leaves the window after; a CT option misread there would show as a short hold, which
         W148-3's timing reads at the start's own test (5e). In a loop the MR pulse lasts at least NRST's fastest fall, 38.8 us
         (MODEL: 80 nF, 386.1 Ohm, the pull-ups at their weakest, an ideal drain; tCTS's minimum is not printed, taken 0): the controller
         holds VCAP up until it is reset, and only the hold stage's RESET resets it, so the pulse is 39x tMR_W
         W145's CTR1 hold, WITHDRAWN (the history of S5): Equation 2's 82.2 ms held only after a fault longer than 9.54 ms ('To ensure the capacitor is fully discharged, the time period or duration of the voltage fault needs to be greater than 5% of the programmed reset time delay.'),
           which a loop's fault was not shown to last; the TPS37's CTR1 is open again (tCTR(no cap) at most 40 us)
       power-up: the TPS3703 holds NRST low from its VPOR, at most 1.0 V, through its UVLO, 1.2 to 1.7 V: 'When the voltage on V DD is less than the device UVLO voltage but greater than the power-on reset voltage (V POR), the RESET pin will be held low , regardless of the voltage on SENSE pin.' (8.4.2, p.17);
         the TPS37 holds MONRST, so MR, low from its VPOR 1.4 V: 'When the voltage on VDD is less than the UVLO voltage, but greater than the power-on reset voltage (VPOR), the output pins will be in reset, regardless of the voltage at SENSE pins.' (8.3.1.1, p.18), to its 2.7 V minimum, and then 'During the power-on sequence, VDD must be at or above VDD (MIN) for at least tSD before the output is in the correct state based on VSENSE.'
         (7.6 note 4, p.9), tSD 2 ms (p.9); the H743 leaves its own BOR0 reset from 1.62 to 1.71 V rising (Table 116, p.212). The
         hold adds at least 14 ms after MR rises, longer than the TPS37's 2 ms tSD, so the monitor is valid before the controller's
         first instruction: NRST is released 14.0 to 28.04 ms after VDD reaches 2.7 V (tD's minimum; tSD + tCTR(no cap) + tD's maximum,
