   5g. THE RESET LOOP (W144's F1): an image that enters VOS1 or VOS0 at every boot. Each cycle it is in VOS1 or VOS0 for at most t_resp
       (S2) at the 1.3144 W step, then in reset; the reset and the boot are taken at no more than the bounded state's power (ASSUMPTION: the
       reset state, VOS3 with the reset clocks and every peripheral at reset, RM0433 p.279, inside FW-B20's bound)
         the hold stage (SESSION W148-1): every cycle's MR pulse lasts at least 38.8 us, over tMR_W's 1 us minimum (5d), so RESET
         asserts and is held for tD after MR returns high, at least 14 ms (7.6, PRINTED), for ANY length of the fault: TI's note B
         starts the counter when MR is high; read by note C instead (the counter from RESET's assertion), the controller is still out of
         VOS1 and VOS0 for at least tD less t_resp. Either way the duty is at most t_resp / tD(min) = 122.6 / 14000 us = 0.876 %, for every
         excursion the monitor registers (W150's F3: an excursion it does not register never reaches the hold, 5i)
         the average rise (W150's F2, MODEL): with T10's own temperature-dependent current (l9t5_t10.py's mcu_i, its leakage feedback),
         the loop's mean junction solves TJ = 76.25 C + 45.0 C/W x 3.3577 V x ((1 - 0.00876) x I(TJ) + 0.00876 x 0.550 A): 101.01 C at I = 0.1605 A,
         a rise of 0.806 K over the bounded state's 100.20 C (W148's 0.518 K held the step at the bounded state and left the feedback out)
         S1's limit at t_resp becomes (105 - 101.01) / (3.3577 V x (0.550 - 0.1605) A) = 3.05 K/W, the step taken from the loop's mean state
         (the average plus one pulse's own rise, a superposition MODEL; W148's 3.25 K/W withdrawn). No fault-length condition on a registered
         excursion: S5 is RETIRED (section 9)
         W145's CTR1 hold, withdrawn (5d): duty 0.212 % and 0.125 K at its t_resp 174.7 us, CONDITIONAL on TI's full discharge (S5)
       U-02's LOCAL AIR AND S1's LIMITS (W150's F1; MODEL on T10's model at the rail's top): the limits above are read at 76.25 C
