   5i. THE SELF-RESET LOOP (W148-F4, given its own row by W150's F3): an image that enters VOS1 or VOS0 and resets itself (a software
       or watchdog reset, RM0433 8.4.2, p.329) before the TPS37 registers the excursion. RESET1 never asserts, so the hold stage never
       runs; the cycle is the image's own: a dwell under the monitor's registration time (unprinted below 20 % overdrive, S2), then the
       internal reset ("The pulse generator guarantees a minimum reset pulse duration of 20 μs for each internal reset source.", p.329), NRST's recharge after the
       pulse generator's unprinted pull, and the boot, none with a printed upper or lower figure but the 20 us. It is a VOS1 or VOS0
       state with a printed current (Table 119), not S-g's kind: W148-F4's classification under row R-2 is withdrawn (row R-4)
       for scale only (MODEL on T10's model, credited nothing): the loop's mean junction reaches 105 C at a duty of 5.34 % at 76.25 C air,
         so 17 us dwells (TPS37 tCTS's printed maximum at 20 % overdrive, used as a size, not a bound) would have to come no oftener
         than every 318 us; at 17 us every 217 us (W150's illustration) the duty is 7.83 % and the mean 107.58 C, 7.38 K over the
         bounded state (W150's open-loop reviewer MODEL: about 7.6 %, about 4.5 K): the whole headroom
       what decides it: whether every excursion an image can make is registered. After the image's own reset the regulator returns to
       VOS3 (p.263) and VCAP falls from VOS1's band to the trip on the controller's own load and its two 2.2 uF; no held page prints
       that fall, and while VCAP stays over the trip SENSE1 still sees the excursion. If the least excursion (the dwell plus that fall)
       is longer than the longest the monitor fails to register, every self-reset becomes the monitor's own loop (S-k, held 14 ms)
       S2 EXTENDED (SESSION W152-3): on the three supervisors of S2 at 76 C and at -40 C, (a) the TPS37's shortest registered
         excursion: VCAP's own ramp to VOS1's band and to VOS0's, cut short by a software reset at stepped delays after the Scale 1
         write, the longest excursion that leaves RESET1 released; (b) VCAP's fall after a reset: the time from the reset to VCAP
         under the trip's least 1.0969 V; (c) 1000 self-reset cycles per supervisor and temperature at the image's earliest reset. Pass:
         the least excursion of (b) at least 2x the longest unregistered excursion of (a), and in (c) every cycle asserts RESET1 and
         holds NRST low at least 14 ms (zero escapes in 3000 per temperature). Fail: the row stays OPEN with a design task (row R-4)
   5h. THE HOLD, COMPARED (W148, on W145's finding W145-F1): what bounds the reset loop's duty for ANY fault length on printed figures
       HS-1 a hold stage after the TPS37 (its RESET1 on the stage's manual reset alone; the stage's RESET onto NRST), two parts read:
         HS-1a TI TPS3808G30 (board B's U221 and U543, SBVS050N): td 180 / 300 / 420 ms with CT to VDD (6.6, p.7, PRINTED); 'A logic low (0.3 VDD) on MR causes RESET to assert.'
           (7.3.3, p.11); 'Once MR is again logic high and SENSE is above VIT + VHYS (the threshold hysteresis), a delay circuit is enabled that holds RESET low for a specified reset delay period.' (7.3.4, p.12): no fault-length condition. The MR pulse that registers: 0.001 us in the TYP column
           only (6.6), MR to RESET 150 ns TYP; its drive prints only 0.4 V at 1 mA (6.5, p.6; board B's D4E-F2 buffers U221 for the same
           reason): through 750 Ohm (peak 4.52 mA, its 6.3 maximum 5 mA, p.5) NRST's fall is bounded at 346.1 us, t_resp 363.5 us; duty
           0.202 %, rise 0.187 K, S1's limit 3.51 K/W at 363.5 us; IC body 2.90 x 1.60 mm (p.1)
         HS-1b TI TPS3703F6050DSER (SBVS249B, held back): tD 14 / 20 / 26 ms with CT to VDD through 10 k (7.6, p.7, PRINTED; option F,
           UV only, SENSE on its own VDD: 'Connect to VDD pin if monitoring VDD supply voltage.', pin functions p.4); the MR pulse that registers: tMR_W 1 us, MIN column
           (PRINTED); its drive 250 mV at 3 mA (VDD 2 V row): t_resp 122.6 us (5d); duty 0.876 %, rise 0.806 K, S1's limit 3.05 K/W
           at 122.6 us; IC body 1.50 x 1.50 mm (p.1); stock: Active in TI's package option addendum
         own faults (both): the stage's RESET stuck released or the series resistor open (no reset: the next test), stuck low (held:
           at once), unpowered (the next test or at once), its timing lost (HS-1a: CT open gives 12 to 28 ms, 6.6; HS-1b: CT open gives
           0.7 to 1.3 ms, found by W148-3's hold timing), CT at ground (HS-1b: TI's latch mode, held at the start's test: at once)
         parts per supervisor: U810, the hold stage, R810, R811, R812, R813, C810, C816 (8; W145's draft 6); the ICs' bodies 8.50 mm2
           (HS-1b) or 10.89 mm2 (HS-1a) per supervisor against W145's 6.25 mm2; board B carries three (Layer 10 lays them out)
       HS-2 one supervisor on VCAP with a printed timeout, no TPS37: TI's TPS3703 window (OV and UV) with its factory-programmed tD
         (A: 140 / 200 / 260 ms with CT to VDD) and tPD at most 30 us at 5 % overdrive (7.6, PRINTED). Its window must hold VOS3's
         printed 0.95 to 1.05 V with both releases outside it and trip under VOS1's 1.15 V (accuracy +-0.7 %, hysteresis up to 0.8 %,
         7.5; a divider can only lower SENSE): of the 13 orderable window codes in the addendum (TPS3703A3250DSER, TPS3703A4080DSER, TPS3703A4110DSER, TPS3703A4330DSER, TPS3703A5075DSER, TPS3703A5085DSER, TPS3703A5120DSER, TPS3703A5180DSER, TPS3703A5330DSER, TPS3703A5500DSER, TPS3703A6330DSER, TPS3703A7330DSER, TPS3703B6050DSER) none fits;
         of Table 12-1's catalogue (24 nominal codes x tolerances 3 to 7 %) 11 fit, none orderable ('minimum order quantities apply.', p.3), the widest a relative
         range of 1.01 % for the divider (0.80 V at 7 %); 1.00 V at 7 % direct: OV release 4.0 mV over VOS3's top, UV release 6.0 mV
         under its bottom, VOS1 7.3 % over the trip; its UV side resets the controller on any VCAP under the window (a constraint on
         a reduced-voltage low-power mode); one part, 4 to 6 per supervisor with its CT pull-up, bypass, series resistor and a divider
       HS-3 no retry: TI's latch mode ('In latch mode, if the RESET pin is low or triggers low, the pin will stay low regardless if V SENSE is within the acceptable voltage boundaries', 'To unlatch the device provide a voltage to the CT pin that is greater than the CT pin comparator threshold voltage, V CT.', 9.1.3, p.20): the first trip holds
         the controller until CT is driven from outside; FW-B23's self-test trips the monitor at every start, so every supervisor would
         latch at its first start unless a peer or a power cycle releases it, an action from outside its failure domain (CON-004)
       READING: HS-1a and HS-1b both bound the loop for any fault length on a printed minimum (180 and 14 ms); HS-1a's registration is
         TYPICAL and its drive slows NRST to 363.5 us; HS-1b's registration is a printed minimum, its drive keeps t_resp at 122.6 us, and
         its shorter hold costs 0.806 K of loop rise; HS-2 needs a non-stock window with margins of a few millivolts; HS-3 breaks the
         self-test or the failure domains. SELECTED (SESSION W148-1, section 7): HS-1b, TPS3703F6050DSER as the hold stage
   VERDICT H-2: NOT SUPPORTED ON PRINTED FIGURES AS A PROOF: the register's end condition ('no printed timing bounds the entry-to-reset
   interval, or the thermal time cannot be bounded on printed figures') is met, since neither the sense delay at VOS0's overdrive (S2)
   nor the controller's transient impedance (S1) is printed. The reset loop's hold no longer rests on an unprinted condition: the
   hold stage's printed minimum bounds its duty for any fault length (5g). It STANDS as the one drafted design that ends every VOS1
   and VOS0 entry whatever the firmware does, on printed thresholds: PROVISIONAL under amendment 1, S1 and S2 supplier tasks with
   pass limits, not a closure. Not claimed: a hardware bar, a printed interval.

6. THE ACCEPTANCE, STATE BY STATE ('the controller inside 105 C in every served state and every state the protection admits'; 105 C is
   VOS0's limit, 125 C VOS1 to VOS3's, Table 113; every figure MODEL on PRINTED unless marked, at one supply corner 3.3577 V, W145-4)
   S-a  the bounded served state (FW-B20, FW-B21, rev V)             105 C     100.20 C (T10 10c's 99.6 C at 3.3 V)                                             HOLDS
   S-b  VOS3 at its printed maximum (200 MHz, all peripherals)       125 C     121.32 C (T10 section 4's 119.4 C at 3.3 V)                                      HOLDS
   S-c  a VOS0 entry by any firmware                                 105 C     ended within t_resp 122.6 us; needs ZthJA(t_resp) <= 3.65 K/W                    CONDITIONAL (S1, S2; C2, C3)
   S-d  a VOS1 entry by any firmware, the self-test included         125 C     ended within t_resp; needs ZthJA(t_resp) <= 19.16 K/W                            CONDITIONAL (S1, S2; C2, C3)
   S-e  the self-test with a dead monitor                            125 C     at most 132.6 us (firmware); needs ZthJA(132.6 us) <= 19.16 K/W                  CONDITIONAL (S1; C2)
   S-f  VOS2 with VCAP under the trip's top (1.05 to 1.1303 V)       125 C     not surely ended by the monitor                                                  OPEN (row R-1, HO-E-REGISTER-ROWS.md)
   S-g  VOS3 above its printed 200 MHz                               125 C     no printed current                                                               OPEN (row R-2, HO-E-REGISTER-ROWS.md)
   S-h  power-up before the monitor is valid                         105 C     NRST held under both UVLOs, then tD (>= 14 ms) after MR rises (5d)               CONDITIONAL (S4)
   S-i  a latent monitor fault, then a firmware VOS0 entry           105 C     a double fault; window at most 3600 s                                            RESIDUAL (single-fault)
   S-k  the reset loop: every excursion the monitor registers, at every boot 105 C     duty <= 0.876 %, rise <= 0.806 K, any fault length; ZthJA(t_resp) <= 3.05 K/W    CONDITIONAL (S1, S2; C2, C3)
   S-l  a latent hold fault (CT's pull-up lost), then the reset loop 105 C     a double fault; W148-3's hold timing (W152-1), window at most 3600 s             RESIDUAL (single-fault)
   S-m  the self-reset loop: an image resetting itself before the monitor registers (W148-F4) 105 C     no printed cadence; S-k's if every excursion registers (5i: S2 extended)         CONDITIONAL (S2 extended, S1; C2, C3; row R-4)
   S-j  any current up to the limiter's 0.5878 A                     as above  a VOS3 state is S-a, S-b or S-g; a VOS1 or VOS0 state S-c, S-d, S-k or S-m       no state outside S-a to S-m
